er processing — so it is born fail-closed in production rather than waiting two trains for P3.4. Consumers thus have a runtime from day one; P3 later adds the worker as the low-latency driver and extends the drain route's duties. **Retention (housekeeping-owned — the worker's timer *and* the drain route's hourly duty from this chunk on, so the degraded topology prunes too; env-overridable):** `events` pruned per-event — only rows **individually receipted (or dead-lettered) by every active consumer** AND older than 90 days, never floor-driven; receipts prune with their events; completed wakeups, delivery ledgers (once P5.1 exists), failure rows, and dead letters pruned after 30 days; the SSE replay window (P5.2) is therefore bounded by wakeup retention.
